Who are we?
SupportYourApp is an international Intelligent Support-as-a-Service company that has been providing business process outsourcing services to IT companies around the globe for the past 15 years. We have 1500+ people in our international community.
We operate globally, supporting clients in 60 languages and partnering with industry leaders like MasterCard, Calm, and MacPaw. With international hubs and coworking spaces around the world, we develop innovative products like Quidget and continuously work to improve the customer experience.
About the role:
We are looking for an AI Solutions Engineer to join our team and lead the design and implementation of AI-powered solutions for customer support and business operations.
In this role, you will translate business and operational requirements into scalable technical solutions, design AI architectures, evaluate technologies and integrations, and guide solutions from discovery through implementation.
You will work closely with clients, internal teams, and technical stakeholders to identify the right AI approach for each use case and ensure that solutions are reliable, scalable, and aligned with business goals.
What you will do:

• Design end-to-end AI solutions based on client business and technical requirements;

• Define solution architecture, integrations, data flows, and implementation approach;

• Design and implement AI-powered solutions, including conversational AI, chatbots, agent assist, and automation;

• Work with LLMs, RAG, prompt engineering, AI agents, and knowledge retrieval systems;

• Lead technical discovery and solution design sessions with clients and internal teams;

• Conduct demos of proposed AI solutions and explain their functionality, capabilities, and business value;

• Troubleshoot technical issues and drive solutions through to resolution.

What you need to succeed in this role:

• Fluency in English (C1+ / Advanced+);

• Practical experience taking an AI support solution from implementation/configuration to actual use by customers or support teams;

• Experience implementing AI-powered chatbots and voicebots specifically for customer support or customer service operations;

• Hands-on experience with AI and automation platforms (for example, Zendesk AI Agents, n8n, Voiceflow, Botpress, Cognigy, or similar tools);

• Understanding of LLMs, Generative AI, RAG, prompt engineering, and AI agents;

• Basic understanding of APIs, integrations, databases, and system architecture;

• Ability to translate business requirements into scalable technical solutions and communicate technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.

Will be an advantage:

• Hands-on experience with helpdesk platforms (for example, Zendesk, Freshdesk, and Intercom), including their automation and AI features;

• Experience with AI evaluation, monitoring, and guardrails;

• Experience working directly with clients during technical discovery and solution design;

• Experience leading implementation projects.

Benefits and Perks:

• Providing services during business hours;

• Opportunity to cooperate fully remotely;

• Inclusive international environment;

• Compensation in USD;

• Rewards for referring friends;

• Balance between project workload and personal time, but also - internal health policy;

• Responsive leadership interested in your growth and long-lasting cooperation;

• Greenhouse conditions for self-development;

• A culture built on trust, with no time-tracking requirements.

*The items listed in this section may vary depending on the terms of your engagement. Certain benefits and conditions typically apply to employees; independent contractors may not be eligible for all of these. The specific terms, including compensation, benefits, and work conditions, will be clearly defined in your agreement if selected.
You can learn more about the company and its culture by visiting our official website and social pages on Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn

About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

About WPP Media&nbsp;

WPP is the creative transformation company. We use the power of creativity to build better futures for our people, planet, clients and communities. For more information, visit wpp.com.&nbsp;

WPP Media is WPP’s global media collective. In a world where media is everywhere and in everything, we bring the best platform, people, and partners together to create limitless opportunities for growth. For more information, visit wppmedia.com&nbsp;

At WPP Media, we believe in the power of our culture and our people. It’s what elevates us to deliver exceptional experiences for both our clients and each other. In this role it will be critical to embrace WPP &amp; WPP Media’s shared core values:&nbsp;

• Be Extraordinary by Leading Collectively to Inspire transformational Creativity.&nbsp;

• Create an Open environment by Balancing People and Client Experiences by Cultivating Trust.&nbsp;

• Lead Optimistically by Championing Growth and Development to Mobilize the Enterprise.&nbsp;

Life at WPP Media &amp; Benefits &nbsp;

Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we’re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.    &nbsp;

WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process. &nbsp;

Please read our Privacy Notice &nbsp; for more information on how we process the information you provide. &nbsp;

Category: IT Services

Location: Fort Western Province Sri Lanka

For an international organization, we are urgently looking for a REMOTE (Senior) SharePoint / Microsoft 365 Consultant. Candidates need to be fluent in English. All positions are long-term. This position is open for freelancers and employees.

Candidates need to be able to work 4 hours per day in the normal office hours in Spain. Europe,

Tasks and Responsibilities:

• Develop SharePoint Online custom client-side web parts using SPFx development toolchain;

• Develop SharePoint Server custom server-side web parts using Visual Studio and Microsoft .Net Framework;

• Develop scripts for the automation of tasks for SharePoint Online (PnP) and SharePoint Server 2016/2019 (PowerShell) deployments;

• Provide web application development support;

• Provide detailed documentation of changes and manage version control with the available systems (Git/GitLab);

• Provide SharePoint knowledge transfer to Client’s technical support personnel;

• Apply software development best practices;

Profile

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +3 years developing functionalities for Microsoft SharePoint 2013

• Excellent knowledge of Visual Studio and Microsoft .Net Framework

• Excellent knowledge of Front-End development with React and Typescript/javascript;

• Self-starter able to dive in, resolve ambiguity, and achieve results;

• Course or certificate in SPFx framework;

• Fluent English;

Offered :

• A challenging role for an international organization;

• Attractive salary package or freelance rate;

Interested :

Please forward your motivation and resume to or call us on +94 114312515 for more information.

